  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nA ridge of high pressure will remain over Utah through the \nextended period. Temperatures will be 5-10 degrees above normal \nwith lower valleys in the low 100s Saturday. Monsoon moisture \nwill reach far SE Oregon and southwest ID south of the Snake \nBasin on Saturday afternoon and continue through early next \nweek. Current forecast does not reflect this but there will be a\nslight chance of thunderstorms along the NV border on Saturday \nand Sunday afternoons. Westerly flow will suppress the ridge on \nMonday, bringing slightly cooler temperatures with dry and \nbreezy conditions. Smoky conditions will continue from area \nwildfires which may keep temperatures slightly cooler than \nforecast.",
